      "id": 1,
      "text": "In 1505, Radom hosted a Sejm session that enacted the Nihil novi act, a landmark in Polish constitutional history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Masovian_Voivodeship",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Historically, the southern part of Radom belonged to Lesser Poland, reflecting the region’s shifting borders.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Masovian_Voivodeship",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "More than twenty percent of Radom’s area is covered by pine and oak forests, making it a green oasis in the plains.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Masovian_Voivodeship",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Radom’s old center, with its preserved streets and parks, is a living museum of the city’s medieval past.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Masovian_Voivodeship",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Radom sits in the Masovian Voivodeship, the same province that houses Poland’s capital, Warsaw.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Masovian_Voivodeship",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "During the interwar period, Radom became a key industrial hub as part of Poland’s Central Industrial Region.",
